# Quick Test - TQUIK (the plan's TQUICK: a NAME is five characters), a TEST course (SPEC.md 130.54.2): the
# BZDEV=1 build's alone, after the shipped courses (the Makefile's BZ_TESTCRS), on no pad, with no shipped
# demo.  "Exits and the save" (docs/plans/BOUNCE-BONANZA-SOAK.md): the GOAL course the rows' launches end on,
# as small as a course can be and still carry what their legs need -
#  - A, the start plate, B a ramp down along +x, C the foot whose last column is the GOAL: the autopilot's
#    play reaches it in 165 steps (3.0 s), no fall (a goal, a replay's end, a best, a saved play);
#  - a CHECKPOINT flag on C, on the route, and a HOLE beside it (a ball poked into it respawns at the flag);
#  - a plain KEEP tube under a block on A, off the route: its IN cell (6, 7) a DRAIN a row pokes
#    the ball into (it is HIDDEN until the OUT cell (3, 7) gives it back: 16 steps, as MILL's drop);
#  - `palette 0` (10h, not the BIOS's 30h: the CGA's colour select is seen) and a short `limit` (a TIMEOUT is
#    waited out in 8 s); the finish clock beside C.
#  - C's front goal cell (14, 7) a HIDDEN exit 1 (2026-11-20): the key of the test map's SECRET route
#    (pathdev.bbc, SPEC.md 130.54.6), so the secret leg plays a shipped tree's course with no patch.
course TQUIK "Quick Test"
test             # SPEC.md 130.54: a test course - no pad, no shipped demo, no target owed
music fairway    # SPEC.md 130.50.3: every course names its song
width 64
ball rubber
uses tube
palette 0
floor rect   3 4  7 9  flat 4             # A, the start plate (a row deeper than B: the tube's body
                                          # stands inside it, no face of it over the void)
wall  rect   3 3  7 4  flat 6             # its back rail
floor rect   7 4 11 8  ramp x 7 11 4 2    # B, down along +x
floor rect  11 4 15 8  flat 2             # C, the foot
goal  rect  14 4 15 7  flat 2             # C's last column is the goal (exit 0) ...
goal  rect  14 7 15 8  flat 2 exit 1 hidden   # ... but its front cell, a HIDDEN exit 1 (the test map's
                                          # secret route, SPEC.md 130.54.6; off the route, a row pokes it)
hole  tile  12 7                          # a pit in C, off the route
checkpoint 12 5                           # flag 0, on the route
wall  rect   4 7  6 8  flat 6             # the tube's body, a block on A's second row from the front
tube keep 6 7  3 7  out -y                # IN (6, 7), the drain; OUT (3, 7), onto A
start 4 5
way 4 5
way 14 5
limit 8
clock 11 7                                # the finish clock (SPEC.md 130.22.6)
